Business goal: Speak directly to developers who care about draw execution while maintaining FairLend's institutional confidence..
Scene: A desktop landing-page hero mockup with the FairLend nav, a strong serif headline about financing that moves with construction progress, and a right-side product-like visual showing a construction roadmap, milestone cards, draw group brackets, evidence status, and a small licensed brokerage badge over a tasteful Canadian build site image..
Focus: Construction draw management clarity, with brokerage authority as the credibility layer..
Decision being supported: Would developer/operators convert better when the hero visual shows the actual draw workflow instead of only a finished building?.
Include: single desktop website hero mockup, roadmap or Gantt-style hero visual, milestone cards, draw group bounding boxes, evidence status chips, licensed brokerage badge, project review CTA, subtle blueprint texture.
Constraints: product UI should be visual and sparse, not a dense dashboard; maintain warm FairLend editorial tone; CTA remains visible above the fold; keep text sparse; use short labels, UI placeholder blocks, or visual markers only when needed; keep the service moment recognizable.
